\newlabel{fig:teaser}{{1}{2}{Stage-3 feature trajectories of a weight-tied ConvNeXt (left) and a standard ConvNeXt-T (right), refined at inference with $\Delta t{=}0.01$ ($T{=}9$; massive channel removed). \textbf {Top:} PCA of all states, paths coloured by depth $t$; white dots mark integer $t$. \textbf {Bottom:} residual speed $\|f(x(t))\|$ (class means; shade: spread). One shared block is a single autonomous field $\dot x = f(x)$; nine independent blocks switch the field at every integer, $\dot x = f_{\lfloor t\rfloor }(x)$. We analyse this contrast throughout the paper}{figure.1}{}}
